# Prelude No. 6 in D minor, Well-Tempered Clavier II, BWV 875
# (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a stormy toccata in three. It opens with a scale rushing
# down an octave and a half, then drumming broken chords; the two hands
# trade the run and the arpeggios, and the music presses on through
# long chains of sixteenths to a chromatic climb and a big close on a
# D pedal. Fiery, but the three-in-a-bar pulse must stay.
#
# Time signature and bars: 3/4, 61 bars, no upbeat; the MIDI has the
# same 61 bars and no repeats (the piece has none). Bar numbers follow
# the MIDI; the Mutopia source's bar-number comments (%5, %10, ...)
# stand before the bar after the one they name.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 116, 183 beats, about 1:37. Track times (MusicBrainz
# track lists): Friedrich Gulda 1:28, about 125; Angela Hewitt
# (Hyperion, 1999) 1:30, about 122; Rosalyn Tureck 1:33 and 1:40 (two
# sets), about 118 and 110; Glenn Gould 1:55, about 95; Edwin Fischer
# 1:19, about 139. 116 is a little under Hewitt: on the chip the
# sixteenths (nearly eight a second) need a fraction more room than on
# a piano to stay distinct.
#
# Structure (from the Mutopia score, checked against the MIDI; the
# section plan is my reading):
#   1-5    the run down the D minor scale, then drumming arpeggios in
#          sixteenths over the bass; a half close on beat 1 of bar 5.
#   5-9    the hands exchange: the run in the left hand (5), rising
#          arpeggios in eighths answered between the hands (6-8).
#   10-17  rising scales in sequence, toward A minor.
#   18-25  over the dominant: a repeated A on top against a rising
#          line (18-21), then turns in thirty-seconds climbing (22-25).
#   26-30  the opening restated in A minor.
#   31-39  sequences, a long held C (34), the figures darkening.
#   40-42  a rising chromatic line in eighths (40-41) to the climax.
#   43-50  falling arpeggio sequences, then a pedal on A (47-50).
#   51-57  running sixteenths, the two hands interlocking, toward the
#          close.
#   58-60  the figure low over the D pedal.
#   61     the final chord, D major, with a fermata.
#
# Range: the bass's low D (D2) of the opening and the close, and other
# notes below B2, are lifted an octave; the D pedal sounds at D3.

tempo 116

voice mid 0          # two parts, mostly

dyn 1 f              # bars 1-4: the opening run and the arpeggios, bold
dyn 5 mf             # bars 5-17: the exchange and the rising sequences
lead 5 bottom        # the run in the left hand
dyn 18 mp            # bars 18-25: over the dominant, quieter
ramp 22-25 mf        # building into the restatement
dyn 26 f             # bars 26-30: the opening in A minor
dyn 31 mp            # bars 31-39: the sequences and the held C
ramp 40-42 f         # bars 40-42: the chromatic climb to the climax
dyn 43 mf            # bars 43-46: falling sequences
dyn 47 mp            # bars 47-50: the pedal on A, holding back
ramp 51-56 f         # bars 51-56: the last build
dyn 57 f             # bars 57-61: the close over the D pedal

rit 3 0.7            # bars 59-61 into the final chord
